    "one_shot": "what a foreground CLI command or a hook would pay to judge even one pair: the model load, then the pair",
    "host": "what a long-lived process pays once, and what it keeps resident; RSS after the rounds drops because macOS compresses idle pages under the memory pressure other processes put on the machine, so read peak_footprint_kb as what the model holds",
    "worker": "the shipped path: the review pass inside `axil worker run`; review_off is the same worker on a byte-identical copy with `[decide] review = false`, which loads no model (and no embedder)"
  },
